  {
   "id": "matematicas-2002-septiembre-6",
   "n": 6,
   "num": 2,
   "bloque": "Opción B",
   "puntos": "2,5",
   "enunciado": {
    "intro": "Calcula \\(\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\frac{3x^3+1}{x^2-x-2}\\,dx\\)",
    "apartados": []
   },
   "solucion": [
    {
     "titulo": "Resolución",
     "html": "<div class='ex'><p>\\(x^2-x-2=(x-2)(x+1)\\) no se anula en \\([0,1]\\). Divido: \\(3x^3+1=(x^2-x-2)(3x+3)+9x+7\\).</p>\\[\\frac{9x+7}{(x-2)(x+1)}=\\frac A{x-2}+\\frac B{x+1}\\iff9x+7=A(x+1)+B(x-2)\\]<p>Con \\(x=2\\): \\(25=3A\\iff A=\\frac{25}3\\). Con \\(x=-1\\): \\(-2=-3B\\iff B=\\frac23\\).</p>\\[\\int_0^1\\left(3x+3+\\frac{25/3}{x-2}+\\frac{2/3}{x+1}\\right)dx=\\Bigl[\\frac{3x^2}2+3x+\\frac{25}3\\ln|x-2|+\\frac23\\ln|x+1|\\Bigr]_0^1\\]\\[=\\frac32+3+0+\\frac23\\ln2-\\frac{25}3\\ln2=\\frac92-\\frac{23}3\\ln2\\]<div class='res'>\\(\\dfrac92-\\dfrac{23}3\\ln2\\approx-0{,}81\\)</div></div>"
    }
   ],
   "clasificacion": [
    {
     "tema": "integ",
     "tipo": "racional",
     "apartados": ""
    },
    {
     "tema": "integ",
